      "heading": "What it leaves to you",
      "html": "<p><strong>It does not walk the site.</strong> Someone has to be there and look.</p><p><strong>It does not sign off the inspection.</strong> The person on the job reads the report and owns it.</p><p><strong>It does not replace competence.</strong> Regulation 7 of the Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999 requires every employer to appoint one or more competent persons to help them meet their health and safety duties. A person is competent if they have &quot;sufficient training and experience or knowledge and other qualities&quot; to help properly with the required measures. Source: <a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1999/3242/regulation/7\">legislation.gov.uk, MHSWR 1999 regulation 7</a>, checked 17 November 2026.</p><p><strong>It does not replace the checks the law asks for.</strong> For example, regulation 8 of LOLER says every lifting operation must be properly planned by a competent person, appropriately supervised and carried out in a safe manner (<a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1998/2307/regulation/8\">legislation.gov.uk, LOLER 1998 regulation 8</a>, checked 17 November 2026).</p><p>A good record makes the competent person faster. It does not stand in for them.</p>"
